cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this paper or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "Symmetry-constrained spectral fibres: reverse-complement group actions on double-stranded DNA and the fibres of circular molecular fingerprints"
abstract: >-
  A strand-agnostic local DNA encoder is constant on the double-stranded fibre, a lattice sum of
  BEST determinants that is #P-hard to evaluate (31,925,753,246,212 members for phiX174 at k = 10).
  On substituted linear chains the radius-r Morgan (ECFP) partition equals the reversal-symmetric
  window spectrum with the substituent at distance r coarsened to its atom type, verified
  exhaustively with RDKit; distinct molecules with identical ECFP4 and ECFP6 are constructed, with
  the bound on the linker length attained.
